in Plaza","shopCentreNameTc":"德田廣場","shopCentreNameSc":"德田广场","thumbnailPath":"/linkweb/api/file/ShopCentrePhoto/ttnxc2/link-reit-business-asset-tak-tin-plaza.jpg?v=742140663a799d99f35ebba4e98359b9"},{"shopCentreId":127,"propCode":"smpxd2","shopCentreNameEn":"Sau Mau Ping Shopping Centre","shopCentreNameTc":"秀茂坪商場","shopCentreNameSc":"秀茂坪商场","thumbnailPath":"/linkweb/api/file/ShopCentrePhoto/smpxd2/link-reit-business-asset-sau-mau-ping-shopping-centre.jpg?v=e9c53cb0991d7ef1158c857a3b253692"}]},"sightseeingNearby":{"titleEn":"Sightseeing Nearby","titleTc":"鄰近觀光景點","titleSc":"邻近观光景点","sightseeings":[{"siteNameTc":"","siteNameSc":"","siteNameEn":"","siteDescriptionTc":"茜草灣原為堆填區，經過翻新後成為現在的遊樂場，倡導可持續廢物處理的新思維。遊樂場佔地3公頃，設有綜合草地，跑步徑及遊樂場，表面與一般康樂設施無分別，底下原來是填有160萬噸棄置廢物，以管理系統控制廢物氣體及溢出物，實在大有乾坤。其他環保特點建築還有風力發動機、太陽能電子版，可為公園及鄰近街燈發電。至於地面排水收集缸、安全軟墊及通道均採用回收物料建設，環保意識可見一斑。","siteDescriptionSc":"茜草湾原为堆填区，经过翻新後成为现在的游乐场，倡导可持续废物处理的新思维。游乐场占地3公顷，设有综合草地，跑步径及游乐场，表面与一般康乐设施无分别，底下原来是填有160万吨弃置废物，以管理系统控制废物气体及溢出物，实在大有乾坤。其他环保特点建筑还有风力发动机、太阳能电子版，可为公园及邻近街灯发电。至於地面排水收集缸、安全软垫及通道均采用回收物料建设，环保意识可见一斑。","siteDescriptionEn":"Built on a restored landfill site, Sai Tso Wan Recreation Ground is an innovative example of a sustainable waste management solution. The 3-hectare park, featuring a multi-purpose grass pitch, jogging track and playground, is built on top of a site filled with 1.6 million tons of domestic waste. There is a landfill gas control system and leachate management system. Other environmental features include: wind turbine and solar panels to generate electricity for the park and nearby street lighting, surface water collection tank, and safety mats and paved paths make use of recycled materials.","siteImagePath":"/linkweb/api/file/ShopCentrePhoto/katxd2/link-reit-business-asset-kai-tin-shopping-centre-sightseeing-sai-tso-wan-recreation-ground.jpg?v=ea68ff9496a38c95fcddaf498412b870","siteImageAltTextTc":"茜草灣遊樂場","siteImageAltTextSc":"茜草湾游乐场","siteImageAltTextEn":"Sai Tso Wan Recreation Ground"},{"siteNameTc":"","siteNameSc":"","siteNameEn":"","siteDescriptionTc":"藍田公園位於山邊，坐擁九龍東及海港壯麗景色，為鄰近地區最大型的露天公園，遊人閒暇時登上山頂可到觀景台。公園還建有兒童樂園、野餐地及健身徑等設施，一應俱全。","siteDescriptionSc":"蓝田公园位於山边，坐拥九龙东及海港壮丽景色，为邻近地区最大型的露天公园，游人闲暇时登上山顶可到观景台。公园还建有儿童乐园、野餐地及健身径等设施，一应俱全。","siteDescriptionEn":"Built atop a hill with spectacular scenery of Kowloon East and the harbor, Lam Tin Park is the largest park in the neighborhood. A leisurely hike uphill leads to a lookout point. Park facilities include a children’s playground, picnic areas, and fitness trails.","siteImagePath":"/linkweb/api/file/ShopCentrePhoto/katxd2/link-reit-business-asset-kai-tin-shopping-centre-sightseeing-lam-park.jpg?v=60c49725b95d35666ebd1db5b9f47527","siteImageAltTextTc":"藍田公國","siteImageAltTextSc":"蓝田公国","siteImageAltTextEn":"Lam Tin Park"},{"siteNameTc":"","siteNameSc":"","siteNameEn":"","siteDescriptionTc":"鯉魚門一直以有多样化的新鮮海鮮酒樓而聞名，而這漁村有150年歷史之久。時至今日，遊客們能在市場選購新鮮的海鮮並且即興烹調享用。鯉魚門依舊是個保留著古色古香的寧靜小漁村，擁有著獨特水上房屋的建築風格。","siteDescriptionSc":"鲤鱼门一直以有多样化的新鲜海鲜酒楼而闻名，而这渔村有150年历史之久。时至今日，游客们能在市场选购新鲜的海鲜并且即兴烹调享用。鲤鱼门依旧是个保留着古色古香的宁静小渔村，拥有着独特水上房屋的建筑风格。","siteDescriptionEn":"Lei Yue Mun is a popular dining destination for fresh seafood. This fishing village dates back at least 150 years. Today, visitors can enjoy selecting the day’s fresh catch straight from the market and have it deliciously served up on the table in no time. Lei Yue Mun retains the quaint charm of a sleepy fishing village with its distinctive village architecture featuring buildings jutting above the water on stilts.","siteImagePath":"/linkweb/api/file/ShopCentrePhoto/katxd2/link-reit-business-asset-kai-tin-shopping-centre-sightseeing-lei-yue-mun.jpg?v=394d1508f569f497aebe87398b43d3a3","siteImageAltTextTc":"鯉魚門","siteImageAltTextSc":"鲤鱼门","siteImageAltTextEn":"Lei Yue Mun"},{"siteNameTc":"","siteNameSc":"","siteNameEn":"","siteDescriptionTc":"路線為全長9.3 公里，從衛奕信徑的第三段起步，走222米即可到達魔鬼山，享受環山美景，把清水灣及東龍洲盡收眼底。沿途可探索古砲遺跡，繼而登上黑山，下山中途經清水灣道可前往井欄樹村，本段由藍天地鐵站為起點。","siteDescriptionSc":"路线为全长9.3 公里，从卫奕信径的第三段起步，走222米即可到达魔鬼山，享受环山美景，把清水湾及东龙洲尽收眼底。沿途可探索古炮遗迹，继而登上黑山，下山中途经清水湾道可前往井栏树村，本段由蓝天地铁站为起点。","siteDescriptionEn":"A 9.3km-long hike along Section 3 of Wilson Trail will take the hiker up 222 metres to Devil’s Peak with its panoramic views of Clearwater Bay and Tung Lung Chau. Along the way, stop by and explore an old fort, ascend further to Black Hill before heading down to Tseng Lan Shue village on Clear Water Bay Road. This section starts from Lam Tin MTR station.\n","siteImagePath":"/linkweb/api/file/ShopCentrePhoto/katxd2/link-reit-business-asset-kai-tin-shopping-centre-sightseeing-wilson-trail-section-three.jpg?v=7c9f8b1e3a219cbd0255316b110587c8","siteImageAltTextTc":"衞奕信徑第 3 段","siteImageAltTextSc":"衞奕信径第 3 段","siteImageAltTextEn":"Wilson Trail Section 3"}]}}}